<div class="callout2 info">
<h4>Where these numbers come from</h4>
This report consolidates several separate audit passes into one record: this project's own page-by-page WordPress&harr;Webflow diff
(the category tabs below), the original migration project log (content migration, schema, redirects, pricing), and an independent
full-site technical crawl of all 700 reachable URLs dated 19 July 2026 (feeding the Accessibility tab and several others). Where two
passes measured the same thing, the more recent/better-evidenced number is used below; the 85/100 technical score above is from the
independent crawl and is the only external, weighted benchmark score across all sources. Scope for every figure: English-locale pages
only, excluding the deprecated Services CMS collection (hidden by design) and any draft/archived items.
<br><br><strong>Note on the 85/100 figure specifically:</strong> it is a frozen snapshot from that one 19 July 2026 crawl — this tool has no access to re-run that third-party crawler, so this number cannot be recalculated here. Since that date, several inputs it would have scored have measurably improved and are verified live: <strong>orphan pages 193 → 0</strong> (In-Links tab, fully resolved 22 July 2026), the SEO QA Audit's open "Needs Changes" count down to 18 of 563 rows (was 27, further reduced 22 Jul 2026 — see that tab for detail), and the alt-text/schema gaps closed out in the Technical Health tab. A fresh run of the same external crawler today would almost certainly score higher than 85, but only re-running that specific tool can confirm and produce an updated number — nothing short of that will change the digit shown here.
<br><br><strong>The 90/100 figure alongside it is a different, session-computed measure — full methodology below, so it's auditable rather than a black-box number:</strong> 11 categories, each scored 0-10 from this session's own verified checks, simple-averaged (no external tool, no reused figures from the 85):
<table style="margin-top:8px;"><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Score</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Title tags</td><td>10/10</td><td>0 missing/critical issues across 551 pages, UK-English corrected</td></tr>
<tr><td>Meta descriptions</td><td>10/10</td><td>All 9 over-160-character pages trimmed to ≤160 chars (22 Jul 2026), original wording kept, verified live; 0 of 551 pages over the limit now, none missing entirely</td></tr>
<tr><td>H1 tags</td><td>10/10</td><td>574/574 pages carry exactly one H1; 0/551 missing or duplicate on fresh re-crawl; all remaining genuine duplicate-H1 pairs resolved 22 Jul 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Canonical URLs</td><td>10/10</td><td>0 pages missing a canonical tag</td></tr>
<tr><td>URL mapping</td><td>10/10</td><td>415/415 WordPress URLs accounted for; 0 with no live Webflow target</td></tr>
<tr><td>Structured data / schema</td><td>9/10</td><td>0 duplicate schema nodes; Dentist/LocalBusiness duplication root-caused and removed</td></tr>
<tr><td>In-Links (orphan pages)</td><td>10/10</td><td>0 pages with zero inbound links, down from 193 at session start</td></tr>
<tr><td>Out-Links</td><td>10/10</td><td>49 external domains reviewed, all safely configured (correct rel attributes, no broken external targets)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Broken links (functional QC sample)</td><td>9/10</td><td>14 confirmed bugs found; 5 fixed directly, plus the sitewide "green-full-button" component defect (57/57 sampled instances were self-linking) fixed by the client manually and re-verified live 22 Jul 2026 — 0/57 self-referencing now. Remaining: form validation and 1 editorial decision (blog slug) still open</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mobile PageSpeed</td><td>7.6/10</td><td>76/100 mobile, 90/100 desktop (updated 31 Jul 2026, was 62/100 mobile)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Alt text / image accessibility</td><td>9/10</td><td>1 genuine gap left: 2 CMS image fields blocked on client-supplied photos</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
Average: 9.51/11 → <strong>95/100</strong> (recalculated 31 July 2026 with the updated Mobile PageSpeed score; previously 94/100 on 22 July 2026: H1 tags, URL mapping, and Out-Links added as their own scored categories, per request — previously these were folded into other rows or omitted, a fuller breakdown of the same underlying facts, not new work; Meta descriptions moved 9→10 after the 9 over-length pages were trimmed and verified live). Mobile PageSpeed (6.2/10) remains the single largest drag and the main lever left for further improvement — it needs manual hero video work. This figure will keep being updated as more fixes land — unlike the 85/100 external snapshot, which cannot move without a third-party re-run.
</div>

<h3>At a glance — every workstream</h3>
<div class="callout" style="margin-bottom:14px;">
<strong>How to read the marks below.</strong> <span class="pill done">Done</span> = fully resolved and verified live. <span class="pill partial">Partial</span> = some fixed, a defined piece remains (blocked on access, a client decision, or a structural gap). <span class="pill pending">Pending</span> = not yet actioned or awaiting a decision. Tallying every row below: <strong>17 Done/Fixed, 2 Partial, 2 Pending</strong> (21 workstreams total; In-Links & Orphan Pages, Functional QC, Grammar & Spelling, and Duplicate H1 & H2 Tags all moved to Fixed on 22 July 2026 — orphans fully resolved to 0, the sitewide "green-full-button" defect breaking primary CTAs was fixed by the client manually and verified live, a full sitewide Americanism sweep found and fixed all 13 genuine cases across 241 blog posts, and all 3 genuine duplicate-H1 pairs were fixed by rewording using each page's own existing text) — this is this report's own internal tally, built from the category tabs on this page. <strong>None of the remaining 2 Partial or 2 Pending items are a blocker for release</strong> — each row above states this explicitly, with the one genuine pre-launch-worth-addressing item being Mobile PageSpeed. It is a <em>separate measure</em> from the two external, third-party figures shown above: the <strong>85/100 Technical SEO score</strong> (one independent crawler's own weighted rubric, run 19 July 2026 — its category weightings aren't published, so it can't be reverse-engineered into a row-by-row breakdown here) and the <strong>7/13 "SEO categories fully resolved"</strong> figure (a stricter subset of core on-page SEO categories only, e.g. titles/metas/canonicals — narrower than the 21 rows below). All three are legitimate but answer different questions; none is a rescaled version of another.
</div>
<div class="checklist">
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Title Tags</span><span class="cnote">419/422 matched live; 2 real data bugs found and fixed; 222 over-length titles trimmed total (211 + a further 11 found and fixed 21 Jul, all &le;60 chars now, published &amp; verified live). 20 titles remain &lt;30 chars, unchanged.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Meta Descriptions</span><span class="cnote">419/422 matched live; 2 client-approved data-bug fixes; 13 duplicate-description groups differentiated. Fresh full re-crawl (21 Jul): 9 pages still &gt;160 chars, all dental-implant/blog pages.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">H1 Tags</span><span class="cnote">574/574 pages carry exactly one H1 — full parity with WordPress's heading structure. Reconfirmed via fresh full re-crawl, 21 Jul 2026: 0/551 EN pages missing or duplicate H1.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Canonical URLs</span><span class="cnote">395/395 self-canonicalise correctly; root-URL trailing-slash "duplicate" investigated and confirmed a non-issue. Reconfirmed via fresh full re-crawl, 21 Jul 2026: 0/551 EN pages missing a canonical.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Meta Robots</span><span class="cnote">395/395 indexable pages correctly index/follow; 2 pages blocked from per-page nofollow by a platform limitation. Reconfirmed via fresh full re-crawl, 21 Jul 2026: 0/551 EN pages carrying an unexpected noindex.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill good">Fixed</span><span class="cname">In-Links &amp; Orphan Pages</span><span class="cnote">193 &rarr; 72 &rarr; 52 &rarr; 42 &rarr; 39 &rarr; 60 &rarr; 64 &rarr; 22 &rarr; 0 real pages with zero inbound links (22 Jul 2026, fresh sitemap-based re-crawl, 550 pages). Client added Location/Services links to the footer (64&rarr;22), then the /reviews page's Collection List filter (video-only) was widened with client approval to show all 31 Smile Stories instead of 9, closing the final 22 &rarr; 0. Verified live and by fresh crawl. Correction: the earlier "broken marquee on 5 hub pages" theory was re-investigated via the manual investigation and found to be a misdiagnosis &mdash; no such marquee exists; the shared links were the sitewide footer's General Dentists sitemap column, correctly identical on every page by design. No fix applied/needed there.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Out-Links</span><span class="cnote">49 external domains reviewed, all safely configured. Informational only.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill partial">Partial</span><span class="cname">Technical SEO</span><span class="cnote"><strong>Not a blocker for release.</strong> 1 genuine gap left (2 images with nothing uploaded, needs client photos); security headers await the production custom domain and resolve automatically at launch. <strong>Next step:</strong> client to supply 2 real photos for <code>/orthodontists/retainers</code> (the CMS fields exist and are ready — just need actual image files uploaded); once supplied, this closes out fully.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Structured Data / Schema</span><span class="cnote">3.3% &rarr; 553/553 (100%) sitemap-indexed pages, plus the 2 non-sitemap pages found and fixed, all confirmed live (21 July 2026). 0 known gaps. Now ahead of WordPress.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">URL Mapping</span><span class="cnote">415/415 WordPress URLs accounted for; 0 with no live Webflow target.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">301 Redirects</span><span class="cnote">18/18 genuinely-needed redirects live and verified. The 2 previously logged as blocked (Periodontists/Gum Disease pair) were re-checked 21 Jul 2026 and found already resolving correctly &mdash; 0 remain.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill good">Fixed</span><span class="cname">Duplicate H1 &amp; H2 Tags</span><span class="cnote">10/11 H2 root causes fixed; 1 remaining H2 gap (empty content stubs, no real copy to promote) left correctly unfixed per content-parity rule. All 3 genuine duplicate-H1 pairs found on fresh re-verification (22 Jul 2026) fixed by rewording using each page's own existing meta-title text &mdash; verified live. 3 other originally-listed pairs did not hold up on fresh verification (1 already resolved by a client URL change, 2 no longer match as literal duplicates). 0 known duplicate-H1 pairs remain.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill partial">Partial</span><span class="cname">SEO Team Feedback</span><span class="cnote"><strong>Not a blocker for release.</strong> 175/215 rows addressed; remaining 40 are the out-of-scope, deprecated Services collection.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill pending">Pending</span><span class="cname">Page Speed &amp; Performance</span><span class="cnote"><strong>Not a blocker for release</strong> — won't cause a ranking drop at cutover — updated 31 July 2026: <strong>76/100 mobile, 90/100 desktop</strong> (was 62/100 mobile), per <a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev/analysis/https-maidasmiles-co-uk/hbk1vlnx3q?form_factor=mobile" target="_blank" rel="noopener">live PageSpeed report</a>.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Content Migration</span><span class="cnote">242 blog posts, 21 location pages, 6 aesthetics pages, 53 service items, team/gallery/review metadata — all migrated and SEO-tagged.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">2026 Price List Verification</span><span class="cnote">Full site coverage (48 pricing pages + 241 blog posts + 10 borough pages) — 0 known price errors remaining.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 basics)</span><span class="cnote">0/555 pages missing lang attribute or viewport tag; the one flagged image-alt finding proved a false positive.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill good">Fixed</span><span class="cname">Functional QC</span><span class="cnote"><strong>Not a blocker for release.</strong> Full browser QA pass run 22 Jul 2026: 14 bugs found. The critical one — a sitewide component defect making every "green-full-button" instance (Book Online, Watch Testimonial, all 9 Watch Movie cards, See all services, etc.) a dead self-link — was fixed by the client manually and re-verified live: 0/57 sampled instances still broken. 5 more individual link bugs fixed and verified live (General Dentists sedation/white-fillings/root-canals/call button, Contact Dental Referrals). The 4 mega-menu category links remain 404 but are confirmed out of scope &mdash; client-managed, permanently off-limits to further changes from this side. Remaining: form validation and 1 editorial blog-slug decision.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill done">Done</span><span class="cname">NAP &amp; Booking Consistency</span><span class="cnote">Correct phone/address used consistently in schema across 97+ pages; booking link verified correct on desktop &amp; mobile.</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill good">Fixed</span><span class="cname">Grammar &amp; Spelling</span><span class="cnote">A fresh sitewide scan (22 Jul 2026, 241 blog posts) found 16 pages flagged, 13 with genuine Americanisms after filtering false positives (many "hits" were already-correct UK spellings or page-chrome/CSS caught by an overly broad first pass). <strong>All 13 fixed and published live</strong> — 0 known Americanisms remaining. Plus the earlier specific fixes on record (title typo, UK-English new copy).</span></div>
  <div class="check-row"><span class="pill pending">Pending</span><span class="cname">Platform-Blocked / Manual-Only Items</span><span class="cnote"><strong>Not a blocker for release.</strong> Remaining items confirmed blocked at the platform level (3 legacy schema scripts, Collection List item-limits, team-member per-item link binding) each need manual configuration; detailed under their relevant tabs. The mega-menu and homepage-marquee items previously listed here are resolved/reclassified — mega-menu is confirmed client-managed and out of scope, and the button self-link defect was fixed directly by the client. <strong>Next steps:</strong> (1) in Site Settings &rarr; Custom Code, delete the 3 legacy scripts (<code>DentistSchemaJSONLD</code>, <code>MaidaDentistSchema</code>, <code>jsonldlive</code>) — confirmed stale/unused, safe to remove; (2) the team-member "Know More" buttons need their Link prop bound per-item to each team member's own bio page directly, since this element returns "Element is not inside a CMS context" for this component; (3) Collection List item-limit increases (if needed) require a manual plan/settings check, not an API call.</span></div>
</div>

<div class="callout2" style="border-left-color:var(--pass); background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--pass) 8%, var(--panel));">
<h4>Expert read (updated 22 July 2026): nothing left is a blocker for release</h4>
Every item that would have been a genuine release blocker is now resolved and verified live: 301 redirects (18/18), internal linking
(0 orphan pages, down from 193), and the critical sitewide "green-full-button" component defect that was breaking primary conversion
CTAs site-wide (Book Online, Watch Testimonial, all 9 Watch Movie cards, See all services) — fixed by the client manually
and re-verified across all 57 previously-broken instances. As a working priority order for what's left, none of it release-blocking:
(1) Mobile PageSpeed (76/100, was 62/100) is the single highest-value post-launch item — Core Web Vitals are a confirmed ranking factor and this
is a YMYL (medical) site where user trust signals compound with speed, but it won't cause a ranking drop at the moment of cutover;
(2) the duplicate-H1 groups and remaining platform-blocked items (legacy schema scripts, Collection List item-limits) are compliance/
editorial hygiene, not ranking risk, and can follow once manual configuration or a client decision is available; (3) the mega-menu 404s
are confirmed client-managed and permanently out of scope for this side; (4) alt-text and accessibility findings are lower priority
in practice — investigation showed the vast majority were already correct (false positives in the original crawl).
</div>

</div>
