    <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-title-tags"><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🏷️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Done</span><strong>Title tags — carried over intact</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">419 of 422 WordPress pages have a verified, matching title tag live on Webflow — nothing was lost in the migration on this front. (The 3-page gap to the current 422 WordPress count reflects pages added after this table was last rebuilt; a 20-page breadth spot-check on 2026-07-20 found zero regressions, so this is a re-labelling gap, not a known defect.) Two real data bugs were also caught and fixed along the way: a blog post (<code>/blog/snap-in-dentures-benefit</code>) was showing the generic blog-index placeholder title instead of its own, and has since been corrected using only the post's own content; a second independent crawl (19 Jul) separately flagged 229 pages with titles over 60 characters and 21 under 30 — 211 of the over-length titles were trimmed on 20 July (character-count edits only, original wording kept, per the client's explicit instruction). <strong>Fresh full re-crawl of all 551 EN pages (21 July 2026, entity-decoded character counts):</strong> confirmed the trim landed, then found 11 titles still over 60 characters (down from 229) — 10 team-member bio pages sharing one "Name | Role | Maida Smiles (W. London)" pattern, plus 1 location page (Kensington veneers). <strong>Client re-authorized a targeted trim of exactly these 11 on 21 July 2026</strong> (character-count only, original wording kept — the same standard as the earlier 211-title pass): the repeated "(W. London)" suffix was dropped from the 10 team pages, "Experienced" was dropped from Mariya Dolhova's (still 70 chars after the suffix trim alone), and "Dental" was dropped from the Kensington veneers title. <strong>All 11 fixed, published, and verified live</strong> — every one now ≤60 characters, confirmed via a fresh curl of each page, then independently reconfirmed with a second full 551-page re-crawl: <strong>0 titles over 60 characters site-wide.</strong> 20 titles remain under 30 characters (unchanged, never in scope for either trim pass). Per standing project rule, title/meta text that has already been set is otherwise a completed, separate workstream — no further rewriting planned beyond this authorized batch.</div></div></div>
        
        
        
