    <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-meta-descriptions"><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">📝</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Done</span><strong>Meta descriptions — carried over intact</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">419 of 422 WordPress pages have a matching, verified meta description live on Webflow. Two client-approved data-bug fixes were made outside the normal scope (meta-title/description edits are otherwise off-limits under the content-parity rule): <code>/team/dr-avadanei</code> had been showing a different dentist's description (copied from Dr Claudia Lorenzo's entry) and now correctly references Dr Avadanei; <code>/blog/snap-in-dentures-benefit</code> had the generic blog-index placeholder text and now uses wording drawn only from its own real body content. A second independent crawl (19 Jul) found 9 pages with descriptions over 160 characters and 13 duplicate-description groups across the location × treatment matrix — differentiated copy was written for the genuinely distinct pages on 20 July; 2 identical pairs (e.g. Smile Gallery vs Photo Gallery) were correctly left alone since they already 301-redirect to one canonical page rather than needing fake differentiation. <strong>Fresh full re-crawl of all 551 EN pages (21 July 2026, entity-decoded character counts) confirms 9 pages remain over 160 characters</strong> — the same count as the original 19 Jul finding, all on dental-implant treatment pages and blog posts, consistent with these being untouched per the standing project rule against rewriting already-set meta text.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">📝</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">New finding — 25 Jul 2026 live verification</span><strong>1 duplicate meta description found (not previously flagged)</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Fresh re-crawl of all 549 pages found 0 missing meta descriptions, 0 over the 165-char limit, but <strong>1 new verbatim duplicate</strong>: <code>/dentures</code> and <code>/invisalign-treatment/invisalign-full</code> share the identical description "As a Platinum Provider of Invisalign Comprehensive in London, we use an unlimited amount of aligners" — looks like an Invisalign-specific description was copy-pasted onto the dentures page in error. Flagging per the literal-duplicate exception in the content-parity rule; the actual text edit is a completed workstream and out of scope for this pass to change unilaterally.</div></div></div>
        
        
        
