    <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-h1-tags"><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🔠</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Done</span><strong>H1 tags — every page has exactly one</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">574 of 574 checked EN pages carry exactly one H1, matching WordPress's single-heading structure and Google's best-practice expectation — re-checked live on 2026-07-17 with no exceptions found. This is a place the Webflow site is provably at parity with WordPress: the historical duplicate-H1/H2 root causes (homepage sections, shared footer/reviews components, CMS templates) are detailed and resolved on the dedicated Duplicate H1 &amp; H2 Tags tab. <strong>Reconfirmed via a fresh full re-crawl of all 551 EN sitemap pages (21 July 2026): 0 pages missing an H1, 0 pages with more than one.</strong></div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">🔠</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">New findings — 25 Jul 2026 live verification</span><strong>Fresh full re-crawl of 549 EN pages: 1 new multi-H1 defect found, 0 missing-H1 confirmed</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Re-crawled all 549 live EN pages directly (curl + HTML parse, not relying on the prior day's crawl dataset, which had a silent extraction bug misreporting 263 pages as H1-less — live-verified those are all fine, exactly one real H1 each). <strong>0 pages found missing an H1</strong>, matching the existing "done" status. <strong>1 new genuine multi-H1 defect found:</strong> <code>/london/marylebone/emergency-dentist</code> has a real H1 plus a second, empty phantom <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> containing only a zero-width joiner character — a stray leftover heading element, isolated to this one page (the other 7 borough × emergency-dentist page combinations were checked and are clean). Not yet fixed, flagged for review. Full detail in <code>scratchpad/live-audit-2026-07-25.md</code>.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🔠</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Fixed — 25 Jul 2026</span><strong>Phantom empty H1 on /london/marylebone/emergency-dentist fixed</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">The stray empty &lt;h1&gt; (zero-width joiner only) was retagged to H2 in place (element not deleted, per the never-delete rule) and published. Page now carries exactly one real H1. <strong>0 known multi-H1 pages remain.</strong></div></div></div>
    
    
    
    
