                    <td class="same">SAME</td>
                    <td class="muted-note">Root-caused 2026-07-16 (corrects the 2026-07-12 note above, which was wrong): this is NOT a WordPress-side issue. Webflow emits a fixed, sitewide "index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1" robots tag on every page (confirmed identical on the homepage, which has no per-page robots setting at all) — Webflow’s page-metadata options have no robots/nofollow field, and this tag is not editable through automated means. Webflow has no native way to serve "nofollow" independent of "noindex". Live-verified unchanged today (curl). Blocked/not fixable via any available method — the WP-vs-WF nofollow/follow difference is a platform capability gap, not a migration bug; restoring nofollow (if desired) would require custom code injection, a manual task.</td>
                    <td><a href="https://maidasmiles.co.uk/blog/dermal-fillers-and-facial-harmonisation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WP</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <a href="https://maidasmiles.webflow.io/blog/dermal-fillers-and-facial-harmonisation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WF</a></td>
