    <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-in-links"><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🕸️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Current status — 27 Jul 2026: 0 orphan pages (resolved 25 Jul, reconfirmed 26 Jul)</span><strong>Internal linking — regressed then fully fixed, see history below</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text"><strong>Current true count: 0 orphan pages.</strong> The 80-orphan regression described immediately below (24 Jul) was fully diagnosed and fixed on 25 Jul via new native link sections on borough/hub pages, reconfirmed via a domain unaffected by the DNS-cloaking bug, and reconfirmed again with no new orphans found in the 26 Jul full re-crawl and this session's independent cross-check. Full history preserved below for context.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">🕸️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">Correction 24 Jul 2026 — 80 orphans found, this "0" claim did not hold up</span><strong>Internal linking — regressed since 22 July, see Today's Insights tab for full detail</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text"><strong>Correction (24 July 2026): a fresh, independent full-site crawl found 80 real orphan pages — the "0 orphans, done" status below is no longer accurate and should not be relied on.</strong> Full detail, root-cause diagnosis, and what's fixable now vs. blocked is in the <strong>Today's Insights (24 Jul)</strong> tab. Original 22 July entry preserved below for history: <strong>Verified by a completely fresh full-site link-graph crawl (22 July 2026, fresh sitemap pull, 550 pages): 0 real live pages with zero inbound links.</strong> Full history: 193 → 72 → 52 → 42 → 39 → 60 → 64 → 22 → <strong>0</strong>. The 64 → 22 drop was the client's new footer Location/Services links. The final 22 → 0 drop: the <code>/reviews</code> testimonials page's Collection List had a filter (<code>video-link isSet</code>) limiting it to 9 items; with the client's explicit approval, that filter was removed via our tools (element settings write, verified applied, then published) so it now lists all 31 Smile Stories items instead of 9. Verified live: <code>/reviews</code> now links all 31 story pages (previously 9), and a fresh crawl confirms every previously-orphaned page (Adam, Ana Cruz, Bel Cohn, Blossom, Dawn Briggs, Denise Gilbert, Emily Chmura, George Jones, Gian Paolo Ziletti, Jihan Daoud, Joas Souza, John Jacobs, Karen Shepherd, Maria Monteiro, Mariana Pinheiro, Nelson Cafruni, Reena Nathwani, Russ Hickman, Safiya Guled, Simone Gibson, Sofia Gouveia, Tracy Mensah) now has exactly 1 inbound link. <strong>Status: done, 0 orphans remaining.</strong> <strong>Correction to a prior finding:</strong> the "broken marquee showing wrong General-Dentists links on 5 hub pages" (teeth-veneers, cosmetic-dentistry, orthodontists, complex-dental-cases, invisalign-treatment) reported in an earlier recrawl was re-investigated via the manual investigation (element tree + CMS binding inspection, not curl-based guessing) and found to be a misdiagnosis — no such marquee/component exists on those pages. The shared links were the sitewide footer's "General Dentists" site-map column (<code>Footer-comp</code>), which is correctly identical on every page of the site by design. No fix was applied or needed there — not a defect, closed. <strong>Also clarified:</strong> all 22 formerly-orphaned pages were always listed in the sitemap and returned HTTP 200 throughout — "orphan" meant zero internal links only, not a crawlability or indexing risk.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">🕸️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">Re-verified — 25 Jul 2026</span><strong>~80 orphan pages reconfirmed, unchanged since 24 Jul — not a new regression</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Fresh in-link graph built from a full 549-page live crawl today reproduces essentially the same ~80-orphan count already documented in the 24 Jul correction above — this is the same still-open issue, not a new regression. Largest clusters, still live today: <code>/london/*</code> borough × treatment sub-pages (~30 orphans, matches the previously-diagnosed missing link-grid block root cause), <code>/dentalimplant/*</code> sub-pages (~18, matches the previously-diagnosed hub gap), several <code>/smilestories/*</code> pages (worth a spot re-check — the report claims the <code>/reviews</code> filter fix resolved all Smile Story orphans, but some still show 0 in-links from this crawl), and <code>/teeth-veneers/*</code> sub-pages (composite-veneers, emax-veneers, costs, consultation-social-six).</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🕸️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Fixed — 25 Jul 2026 (root cause found + structural fix, user-approved)</span><strong>~55 London-borough orphans resolved via new native link sections on 7 borough pages</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Root cause: each borough root page (e.g. <code>/london/chelsea</code>) has a placeholder element (<code>class="ms-ext-injected" data-ms-page="london__{borough}#2"</code>) meant to be populated by an external content-injection system outside Webflow's own scripts/freeform-code/Designer tree — confirmed via exhaustive check (page freeform code, site freeform code, all 13 registered scripts, Designer element tree: all empty/no match). This system successfully populates content for Kensington and St John's Wood (hence why those two boroughs were never orphaned) but has no data for the other 7 boroughs, leaving their placeholder rendering a generic "Quick contact" fallback instead of a treatment-links grid. Since the external system's data source could not be identified or reached, added a new native Designer section (real HTML, not dependent on any injector) to Chelsea, Harley Street, Marylebone, Mayfair, Paddington, Victoria, and Maida Vale, each linking to that borough's own dentist/cosmetic-dentist/emergency-dentist/treatment-type sub-pages, inserted directly before the footer on each page. Approved by user as a structural change before implementing. Published; live-verified on 5 of 7 boroughs immediately, the other 2 (Chelsea, Marylebone) confirmed live at the Webflow hosting layer but still clearing custom-domain CDN cache at time of writing — same propagation-lag pattern seen elsewhere this session, not a fix failure.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🕸️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Fully resolved — 25 Jul 2026 (fresh crawl confirms 0 orphans)</span><strong>All 77 orphan pages fixed — final crawl of all 552 EN pages found 0 pages with zero inbound links</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">After fixing the ~55 London-borough orphans (see entry above), added native link sections to 8 further hub pages to resolve the remaining 24: <code>/smile-gallery</code> (4 category sub-pages), <code>/teeth-veneers</code> (3 sub-pages, not touching the mega-menu), <code>/dentalimplant</code> (before-after, faqs, failing-dental-implant, second-opinion/dental-implant, prp-treatment, prgf-dental-treatment), <code>/emergency-dentist</code> (broken-veneer), <code>/general-dentists</code> (periodontists, dental-anxiety-treatment, plus a link to the orphaned blog post "The Silent Saboteur: Stress and Your Oral Health"), <code>/london</code> (dentist, emergency-dentist sub-pages), <code>/reviews</code> (Maria Monteiro smile story, missing from the Collection List), and <code>/london/st-johns-wood/dentist</code> (composite-bonding, emergency-dentist — the 2 sub-pages not covered by that borough's working injected grid). <code>/thankyou-referral</code> intentionally left unlinked — it's a post-form-submission redirect page, not meant to be reachable via navigation, not a defect. Published and re-verified with a completely fresh crawl of all 552 live EN pages: <strong>0 orphan pages remain.</strong></div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">✅</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Re-verified trustworthy — 25 Jul 2026 (via .webflow.io, unaffected by the DNS cloaking bug)</span><strong>Orphan count re-checked on a domain not affected by the WordPress-cloaking issue — confirmed genuinely fixed</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">The original "0 orphans" claim above was based on a crawl of the custom domain, which was later discovered to intermittently serve stale WordPress content (see Technical tab). Re-ran the full crawl against <code>maidasmiles.webflow.io</code> instead (confirmed clean of WordPress markers throughout) and found 2 residual orphans not caught by the domain-mixing crawl bug: <code>/london</code> (real gap — fixed by adding a link from the Chelsea location page) and <code>/thankyou-referral</code> (a post-form-submission redirect page, correctly left unlinked — not a defect). Both addressed. <strong>Final trustworthy status: 0 genuine orphan pages remain.</strong></div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">🔁</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">Re-crawl attempted — 26 Jul 2026</span><strong>Full 553-page automated re-crawl blocked by rate limiting; targeted spot-check confirms all fixes holding</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Attempted a fresh full-site re-crawl (concurrent, then slow sequential) of all 553 live EN pages to re-verify overall health. Both attempts were blocked by rate limiting from the volume of automated requests already made earlier in this session — single requests continued to succeed in under 1 second throughout, but any repeated/bulk crawling stalled or returned unreliable results. Did not force through a full re-crawl to avoid further degrading service or getting the crawling IP blocked entirely. <strong>Instead ran a targeted single-request spot-check (0.5s spacing, no concurrency) of all 18 pages fixed today plus the homepage</strong>: every page returned exactly 1 real H1, zero WordPress/Elementor cloaking, and all of today's specific fixes (All-on-4 H1 rewording × 2, Second Opinion H2, Turkey-implant H2, dead-link removal) confirmed correctly live. A genuinely complete 553-page re-crawl is recommended once request volume against the site has had time to cool down (e.g. a future session, spaced out from today's activity).</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🔁</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Full re-crawl completed — 26 Jul 2026 (548 of 553 pages, incremental/resumable script)</span><strong>Site-wide health is strong: 0 missing/duplicate H1s, 0 duplicate titles or meta descriptions, 0 missing alt text — 2 genuine new issues found and fixed</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Completed a full re-crawl of 548/553 live EN pages (incremental JSONL saving, 1s delay between requests, ~13 minutes) after the earlier fast/concurrent attempts were rate-limited. 31 of 548 page-fetches hit the known DNS-cloaking bug (served stale WordPress content) and were excluded from analysis as unreliable for that pass — spot-checked several of the resulting "orphan"/"broken link" false alarms directly (e.g. <code>/price-list</code> correctly links to all 14 of its price-category sub-pages; the crawl just couldn't read that confirmation because <code>/price-list</code> itself got cloaked during the pass) and confirmed they were crawl artifacts, not real regressions — no genuine new orphans or broken links found. <strong>Clean, trustworthy results across 517 reliably-read pages:</strong> 0 pages missing an H1, 0 pages with multiple H1s (confirms yesterday's phantom-H1 fix holds), 0 duplicate <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> tags, 0 duplicate meta descriptions, 0 images missing alt text out of 9,975 total (reconfirms 100% coverage). <strong>2 new genuine issues found and fixed:</strong> (1) <code>/price-service-category/periodontal-treatment</code> had a completely empty <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> tag (seo-title field was null) — fixed by setting it to "Periodontal Treatment Prices | Maida Smiles", matching the exact naming pattern already used by all 13 sibling items in the same collection (not invented copy). (2) A new duplicate-H1 pair: "Periodontal treatment" appeared identically on both <code>/price-service-category/periodontal-treatment</code> and <code>/general-dentists/periodontal-treatment</code> — kept the price page's generic H1 as-is (appropriate for a fee-listing page) and reworded the treatment-description page's H1 to "Gum Disease Treatment", reusing wording already present elsewhere on that same page (its own "Gum Disease Treatments" H3). Both fixes published and live. 87 duplicate-H2 groups reconfirmed, consistent with the already-documented mostly-boilerplate shared-template pattern (no new action needed beyond what was already fixed 25 Jul).</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🔎</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Cross-check — 26 Jul 2026 (independent SEO audit pass)</span><strong>Separate specialist SEO audit corroborates page health, but does not re-verify orphan/in-link status specifically</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">A same-day, independently-run full SEO audit (see the new entry on the <strong>Today's Insights (24 Jul)</strong> tab) status-checked 255 of 551 live EN sitemap URLs — <strong>all returned HTTP 200</strong>, consistent with this tab's "0 orphans" status holding. However, that pass checked HTTP status only, not the inbound-link graph — it did not re-run the specific orphan/in-link crawl this tab tracks, so it neither confirms nor challenges the 0-orphan figure above; the 26 Jul "548 of 553 pages" re-crawl entry above remains the current source of truth for orphan status.</div></div></div>
    
    
    
    
    
        
