                    <td class="muted-note">Dentist/LocalBusiness schema duplication: root cause found and fixed — a legacy hardcoded &lt;script src=...maidadentistschema-1.0.0.js&gt; DOM element was live inside the site-wide Header component (id e5d89c7f-9e22-6fd6-e78e-9d3c6455605e, element 969c7077-eccb-2c6d-bc98-8a1e9b8e4b81), injecting a second, stale Dentist JSON-LD block that duplicated/conflicted with the correct site-wide LocalBusinessSchema script. Verified via curl that the file&#x27;s content was a raw Dentist JSON-LD injector; removed the DOM element and republished the site; re-verified via curl on home, a blog post, and a service-style page that maidadentistschema-1.0.0.js no longer loads. Two other legacy registered scripts (jsonldlive, dentistschemajsonld) were checked and are NOT referenced anywhere live (not in site/page scripts, not in header/footer DOM) — they appear to be unused leftover registrations, not a live cause. || Heading-level-skip (H2→H4): root cause found in the shared Footer component (&#x27;Come visit us&#x27; section, component id 74feaa62-60ba-bb14-3f85-1fc08292657e) — H2 &#x27;Book now&#x27; was followed directly by H4 &#x27;Call us!&#x27; / H4 &#x27;View all contact options&#x27;, skipping H3. Changed both to H3 via set_heading_level and published; verified via curl that home, /reviews/, and /smile-gallery/ now render H2→H3→H3 in the footer. Also changed the shared &#x27;Defaut Card 01&#x27; component (196 site-wide instances, used for most H2-then-card-heading sections) default heading level from H4 to H3, which resolves the same skip pattern wherever that component appears under an H2 without an existing per-instance override. Caveat: a few individual instances with an explicit per-instance heading-level override (e.g. the homepage &#x27;Registering as a private patient&#x27; section, where &#x27;Call us!&#x27;/&#x27;View all contact options&#x27; still render as H4 after publish+recheck) were not all individually re-verified 