7;Invalid tag&#x27; error), so these cannot be converted to a non-heading tag. Needs manual fix: replace the Heading elements with Text Block or Link Block elements. Single shared component — fixing once resolves this for the whole site. || Heading-level-skip (H2→H4): root cause found in the shared Footer component (&#x27;Come visit us&#x27; section, component id 74feaa62-60ba-bb14-3f85-1fc08292657e) — H2 &#x27;Book now&#x27; was followed directly by H4 &#x27;Call us!&#x27; / H4 &#x27;View all contact options&#x27;, skipping H3. Changed both to H3 via set_heading_level and published; verified via curl that home, /reviews/, and /smile-gallery/ now render H2→H3→H3 in the footer. Also changed the shared &#x27;Defaut Card 01&#x27; component (196 site-wide instances, used for most H2-then-card-heading sections) default heading level from H4 to H3, which resolves the same skip pattern wherever that component appears under an H2 without an existing per-instance override. Caveat: a few individual instances with an explicit per-instance heading-level override (e.g. the homepage &#x27;Registering as a private patient&#x27; section, where &#x27;Call us!&#x27;/&#x27;View all contact options&#x27; still render as H4 after publish+recheck) were not all individually re-verified — if this specific URL&#x27;s skip is in such a section rather than the standard footer/card pattern, it may need a follow-up spot-check. || Verified live 2026-07-13: heading order correct, nav-menu fix confirmed, schema issues resolved. Meta-title-length flags excluded from scope.</td>
