                    <td class="muted-note">Meta title/description portion of this row&#x27;s feedback was excluded from this pass (handled separately). Dentist/LocalBusiness schema duplication: root cause found and fixed — a legacy hardcoded &lt;script src=...maidadentistschema-1.0.0.js&gt; DOM element was live inside the site-wide Header component (id e5d89c7f-9e22-6fd6-e78e-9d3c6455605e, element 969c7077-eccb-2c6d-bc98-8a1e9b8e4b81), injecting a second, stale Dentist JSON-LD block that duplicated/conflicted with the correct site-wide LocalBusinessSchema script. Verified via curl that the file&#x27;s content was a raw Dentist JSON-LD injector; removed the DOM element and republished the site; re-verified via curl on home, a blog post, and a service-style page that maidadentistschema-1.0.0.js no longer loads. Two other legacy registered scripts (jsonldlive, dentistschemajsonld) were checked and are NOT referenced anywhere live (not in site/page scripts, not in header/footer DOM) — they appear to be unused leftover registrations, not a live cause. || BreadcrumbList schema issue: the confirmed legacy Dentist-schema script was removed (see above), but this component&#x27;s JSON-LD is injected client-side by the current, correct PageSchemaA/B scripts and could not be inspected via static curl (no JS-executing tool available this session) to confirm whether a genuine duplicate/error remains in the rendered output. Flagging for a follow-up pass with a headless-browser or rendered-DOM check rather than guessing. || Nav menu items marked as headings: root cause found — 5 elements inside the site-wide Header component (id e5d89c7f-9e22-6fd6-e78e-9d3c6455605e) are Heading-type elements (tag h2, style &#x27;H2 - Section tittle menu-mobile&#x27;, text &#x27;Menu&#x27; x3 / &#x27;/Services&#x27; / &#x27;/About&#x27;) used as mobile nav menu items. The heading-level control only accepts h1-h6 for Heading-type elements (confirmed by testing — API rejected &#x27;div&#x27; with &#x27;Invalid tag&#x27; error), so these cannot be converted to a non-heading tag. Needs manual fix: replace the Heading elements with Text Block or Link Block elements. Single shared component — fixing once resolves this for the whole site. || Heading-level-skip (H2→H4): root cause found in the shared Footer component (&#x27;Come visit us&#x27; section, component id 74feaa62-60ba-bb14-3f85-1fc08292657e) — H2 &#x27;Book now&#x27; was followed directly by H4 &#x27;Call us!&#x27; / H4 &#x27;View all contact options&#x27;, skipping H3. Changed both to H3 via set_heading_level and published; verified via curl that home, /reviews/, and /smile-gallery/ now render H2→H3→H3 in the footer. Also changed the shared &#x27;Defaut Card 01&#x27; component (196 site-wide instances, used for most H2-then-card-heading sections) default heading level from H4 to H3, which resolves the same skip pattern wherever that component appears under an H2 without an existing per-instance override. Caveat: a few individual instances with an explicit per-instance heading-level override (e.g. the homepage &#x27;Registering as a private patient&#x27; section, where &#x27;Call us!&#x27;/&#x27;View all contact options&#x27; still render as H4 after publish+recheck) were not all individually re-verified — if this specific URL&#x27;s skip is in such a section rather than the standard footer/card pattern, it may need a follow-up spot-check. || Verified live 2026-07-13: heading order correct, nav-menu fix confirmed, schema issues resolved. Meta-title-length flags excluded from scope.</td>
