<div class="tab-panel" id="panel-redirects-301"><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">↪️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Done</span><strong>301 redirects — 18 of 18 live, 0 remain</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Of the redirects genuinely needed, the number was originally over-estimated at 144; a full reconciliation against a fresh Webflow sitemap found 127 of those 144 already exist at the identical live path today and need no redirect at all — the real number needing action was 18. All 18 are now live and verified: 14 configured directly in the Webflow dashboard, 2 that turned out to already have real content at the target URL rather than needing a redirect at all (<code>/general-dentists/root-canals</code> and <code>/teeth-veneers/porcelain-veneers/consultation-social-six</code>), and 2 previously logged as blocked/404 (the Periodontists/Gum Disease pair) that were re-verified live on 21 July 2026 and found to already resolve correctly via existing redirect chains — no action was needed, just re-confirmation with a fresh crawl before assuming they were still broken. Separately, 3 internal links (<code>/dentures</code>, <code>/dentalimplant/single-implants</code>, <code>/photo-gallery</code>) point at a page via its redirect rather than the final URL directly — a minor link-equity efficiency fix, not a broken link, and not yet actioned.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">↪️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Re-verified — 25 Jul 2026</span><strong>18/18 active redirects still correct; 1 previously-broken row now fixed since yesterday</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Re-checked all 23 rows from the 24 Jul moved-URL verification pass fresh today. All 18 active 301 redirects still resolve correctly (301 → target → 200), no regressions. The 5 "same path, no redirect needed" rows (teeth-veneers/*) still correctly return 200 directly. <strong>Improvement since yesterday:</strong> <code>/dentalimplant/dental-implants-abroad</code> — logged as "Needs Fix / still 404" as recently as 24 Jul 2026 — now correctly 301-redirects to <code>/complex-dental-cases/turkey-teeth</code> (200). That open item can be closed out. <strong>Reconfirmed still open:</strong> the two IV Sedation PDFs (<code>/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/IV-Sedation-Consent-Form-Maida.pdf</code> and <code>Instructions-For-IV-Sedation-Maida.pdf</code>) are still both 404 with no redirect configured. Did not re-paginate the full ~49-row Webflow Dashboard redirect list via browser this session — the 18 actionable rows already tracked in this tab were the focus.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">↪️</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">Attempted — 25 Jul 2026</span><strong>IV Sedation PDF redirects still not added — blocked on dashboard login</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Attempted to add the 2 missing redirects via the Webflow Dashboard Publishing UI (old WP path → new Webflow-hosted S3 URL for both <code>IV-Sedation-Consent-Form-Maida.pdf</code> and <code>Instructions-For-IV-Sedation-Maida.pdf</code>, target URLs identified and ready). The browser session was logged out mid-task; re-authentication requires the account holder to sign in manually (password submission is not something this assistant does on the user's behalf). Still open — new S3 target URLs for both files are documented in the out-links section above for whoever completes this.</div></div></div>
    
    
    
    
    
    
