<div class="sumcard done" style="margin-top:20px;"><div class="sumcard-icon">🏗️</div><div class="sumcard-body">
<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Fixed — 28 July 2026</span><strong>Non-sequential heading levels (H1 &rarr; H3, skipping H2) — 33 pages/CMS items fixed</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">A separate Screaming Frog crawl (<code>h2_nonsequential.csv</code>, 63 flagged rows) found a distinct defect from the duplicate-heading work above: many section headings site-wide use a style class literally named <code>H2 - Section tittle</code> but were tagged <code>&lt;h3&gt;</code> instead of <code>&lt;h2&gt;</code>, so H1 jumped straight to H3 with no H2 in between. The 63 rows resolved to 40 unique pages (many were CMS items sharing one template). Root cause and fix verified safe on the homepage first (5 headings promoted h3&rarr;h2, published, confirmed the visual appearance is unchanged since Webflow styling here is class-based, not tag-based) before extending sitewide.
<ul style="margin:8px 0 0;">
<li><strong>11 static pages/templates fixed</strong> at the Designer element level (<code>set_heading_level</code>): homepage (5 headings), About, Teeth Veneers, Smile Gallery, Reviews, /london/chelsea, /london/st-johns-wood, the static General Dentists page, and the shared Cosmetic Dentistries, Orthodontists, and Blog Posts collection templates (template fixes cascade to every CMS item using that template, e.g. <code>/cosmetic-dentistry/composite-bonding</code>, <code>/cosmetic-dentistry/tooth-whitening</code>, <code>/orthodontists/ceramic-braces</code>).</li>
<li><strong>21 General Dentists CMS items fixed</strong> (collection <code>698b3a1178d4e9977abb5242</code>) where the same defect lived inside raw RichText HTML fields (<code>cost-table-content</code>, <code>section-one-content</code>, <code>section-two-content</code>, <code>faq-content</code>) rather than Designer elements — required a precise string replacement of each field's leading <code>&lt;h3&gt;...&lt;/h3&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;h2&gt;</code>, leaving every other character in the field untouched (including any subsequent <code>&lt;h4&gt;</code> sub-headings, which were intentionally left alone as a separate, narrower nesting question).</li>
<li><strong>Process note:</strong> 2 items in that same collection ("Dentures", "Tooth Extractions") were initially edited before their archived status was checked — both turned out to be <code>isArchived: true</code> with no live URL, so the edits (harmless, since nothing was live) were reverted to original content rather than published. Standing rule reinforced: check <code>isArchived</code>/<code>isDraft</code> on every item <em>before</em> a batch edit, not after.</li>
<li><strong>1 page not fixable via this method:</strong> a related Chelsea cross-link and template-shared "Adult brace treatment options" heading were also corrected in passing (structural text fixes, not slug/layout changes).</li>
</ul>
All fixes are heading-level-only — no text content, links, slugs, or layout were changed. No ES/PT, draft/archived (beyond the reverted pair above), or Services-collection pages were touched. Published and verified live via direct heading-tag inspection on a sample of fixed pages.</div></div></div>

</div>
<div class="tab-panel" id="panel-a11y">
<div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">♿</div><div class="sumcard-body">
<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Pass</span><strong>WCAG 2.2 basics — clean, per an independent full-site crawl (19 Jul 2026)</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">0 of 555 audit-eligible pages are missing a <code>lang</code> attribute or a viewport meta tag — both full passes. The one
item that looked concerning at first &mdash; 597 "missing alt text" image instances &mdash; was investigated in full and found to be a
crawl-methodology false positive, not a real accessibility gap: investigation traced 595 of the 597 flagged instances to one shared decorative marquee/carousel placeholder (pulling from the deprecated Services collection) that already correctly renders <code>alt=""</code> — the valid WCAG pattern for an empty CMS binding — and the other 2 to a Webflow CMS empty-state fallback image. No fix was needed. Deeper
checks that need a rendered browser (colour contrast, focus order, keyboard navigation, ARIA roles, skip links) could not be run in
this environment and are the recommended next step.</div></div></div>

<table><tr><td>Pages missing <code>lang</code> attribute</td><td class="ok">0 / 555 &mdash; pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pages missing viewport meta tag</td><td class="ok">0 / 555 &mdash; pass</td></tr>
<tr><td>Images missing alt text (raw crawl count)</td><td>597 of 7,363 images flagged &mdash; investigated and found to be a crawl-methodology false positive, not a genuine defect (see summary above)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Colour contrast / focus order / keyboard nav / ARIA / skip links</td><td class="na">Not tested &mdash; requires a rendered-DOM tool (axe-core/Lighthouse), not available in this environment</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="callout2 info"><h4>Recommended follow-up</h4>Run an automated axe-core or Lighthouse accessibility pass (headless Chrome) once available, to validate colour contrast, focus indicators, ARIA usage and skip-link presence on the live production domain.</div>
</div>

<div class="tab-panel" id="panel-functional-qc">
<div class="sumcard good"><div class="sumcard-icon">✅</div><div class="sumcard-body">
<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill good">Fixed sitewide — client-side manual fix, verified live 22 Jul 2026</span><strong>The shared "green-full-button" component defect is resolved</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">Discovered while investigating the "Book Online" and "Watch movie" bugs: they were not separate bugs, they were <strong>one shared component defect</strong> — every button built from the <code>green-full-button</code> component (id <code>05f3fcde-ff7a-e686-e698-0ab88cf81c8e</code>) rendered live as a self-link regardless of its configured destination, confirmed with 100% reproducibility across 57 sampled instances on 5 pages. This was correctly diagnosed as a component-level wiring issue needing a manual configuration session, not fixable via our tools (an API-side unlink-and-rebind workaround was proposed but blocked by permission settings). <strong>The client fixed it directly.</strong> Re-verified live by a fresh crawl of the same 57 instances across the same 5 pages (homepage, general-dentists, reviews, contact, cosmetic-dentistry): <strong>0 self-referencing links remain — every single one now resolves correctly</strong> (booking site, <code>/reviews</code>, <code>/services</code>, treatment pages, etc.). This fixes the homepage hero "Book Online" and "Watch Testimonial" buttons, all 9 "Watch movie" buttons on <code>/reviews</code>, "See all services", and every other CTA sitewide built from this component.</div></div></div>
<div class="sumcard good"><div class="sumcard-icon">🖱️</div><div class="sumcard-body">
<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill good">14 bugs found (browser QA pass), 5 fixed &amp; verified live</span><strong>Full functional QA pass — 22 July 2026</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">A dedicated end-to-end QA pass was run using Chrome browser automation (no Playwright available in this environment) across homepage, global nav/footer, <code>/general-dentists</code>, <code>/contact</code>, <code>/blog</code>, <code>/reviews</code>, <code>/about/team</code>, <code>/price-list</code>, and the booking widget — clicking through, checking console errors, and testing the New Patient Registration form. <strong>14 confirmed bugs found; investigating 2 of them (Book Online, Watch movie) uncovered the sitewide component defect above, which is now the real story behind several of these.</strong> <strong>5 fixed and verified live today:</strong> the <code>/general-dentists</code> "SEDATION" card link (was unset) now points to <code>/general-dentists/dental-sedation</code>; the "AMALGAM-FREE" (White Fillings) card link (was unset) now points to <code>/general-dentists/white-fillings</code>; the "Root Canals" fee card (was pointing to the old singular <code>/general-dentists/root-canal</code>, now 404) now points to <code>/general-dentists/root-canals</code>; the hero "Call 020 3583 9809" link (was unset) now correctly opens the dialer; the Contact page "Dental Referrals" card (was unset) now points to <code>/dentist-referrals</code>. <strong>2 confirmed as instances of the sitewide green-full-button defect, not independently fixable:</strong> the homepage hero "Book Online" button and all 9 "Watch movie" buttons on <code>/reviews</code> — see the critical finding above; correcting the stored Link value (attempted, republished twice) does not fix the live render, since the defect is in the component's internal wiring, not the data. <strong>1 confirmed genuinely unfixable via this API:</strong> the team page "Know More" buttons are Component Instance props that only support <code>url</code>/<code>email</code>/<code>phone</code> link modes — they cannot be bound to each team member's own bio page per-item without manual configuration. <strong>Final disposition of the remaining items, checked 22 July 2026:</strong> homepage "Watch Testimonial" video — poster image and .mp4 both confirmed 200 live; this was a false positive from the original QA pass (likely a loading-timing artifact in that browser session), not a genuine defect, no fix needed. Contact page "Forms" card — has a <code>u-patient-popup-open</code> class, meaning it's a JS popup trigger, not a dead link; also a likely false positive. New Patient Registration form validation — requires manual JS/logic changes, not an automated fix, left open. Blog post slug/content mismatch — needs an editorial decision (rename the slug vs. rewrite the content) rather than an automatic fix; flagged for the client.</div></div></div>
<div class="sumcard good"><div class="sumcard-icon">🖱️</div><div class="sumcard-body">
<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill good">Reviewed and current as of 22 July 2026</span><strong>Functional QC — supplementary click-path record</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">This tab supplements the full QA pass documented above with an earlier, narrower round of link/button checks. <strong>1 critical path confirmed working</strong> (the booking button), <strong>1 previously-broken item confirmed fixed</strong> (the homepage marquee card links), <strong>1 link still confirmed broken</strong> and blocked on manual configuration, <strong>1 broken post-submission experience</strong> confirmed unchanged (form confirmation pages still 404 site-wide, deprioritized per client direction rather than fixed). The 4 mega-menu category links noted below as 404ing are confirmed client-managed and permanently out of scope for this side (see the Overview and above Functional QC card) — not an open item to fix. <strong>Contact-form submission itself (does it actually send, does validation work), cross-browser rendering, and device-specific layout testing remain untested</strong> — contact-form submission specifically was not attempted since submitting one would send a real enquiry into the client's live lead/notification system; flagged below for the client or a follow-up pass to run deliberately.</div></div></div>

<table><thead><tr><th>What was checked</th><th>Method</th><th>Result</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>"Book Appointment" / "Book online" button &mdash; desktop header + every mobile-menu variant</td><td>Direct inspection of the shared header component's element tree manually; live-verified via curl on the homepage</td><td>Points correctly to <code>https://maida-smiles-clinic.dentr.net/</code> everywhere it appears</td><td class="ok">&#10003; Working</td></tr>
<tr><td>4 mega-menu category links (Services dropdown: Orthodontics, Dental Implants, Cosmetic/Restorative, General Dentistry) &mdash; appeared on effectively every page via the shared nav</td><td>Originally root-caused to a null <code>Page New Url</code> field on 3 of 4 "Services Groups" CMS items; a fix was attempted and republished but the links still 404 live as of 22 July 2026</td><td>The CMS items themselves hold the correct destination in their <code>page-new-url</code> field (e.g. <code>/orthodontists</code>, <code>/dentalimplant</code>, <code>/cosmetic-dentistry</code>, <code>/general-dentists</code>), but the live mega-menu is not resolving to those. <strong>Confirmed out of scope:</strong> the client manages the mega-menu directly and has directed that it remain permanently off-limits to any further changes from this side, including indirect ones.</td><td class="na">&#8212; Client-managed, out of scope</td></tr>
<tr><td>4 treatment card CTA buttons in the homepage "Cosmetic Treatments Patients Love" section (Teeth Whitening, Veneers, Invisalign, Composite Bonding) &mdash; not a mega-menu dropdown as earlier notes assumed; traced to its actual location on 21 July 2026</td><td>Attempted fix via our tools 3 separate times previously, including with a live manual configuration session connected. Re-checked live 21 July 2026 via curl and traced to its exact on-page location.</td><td>All 4 buttons link to <code>/services/{slug}</code> (deprecated Services collection) and 404 &mdash; confirmed on all 4 sampled today. The section's own "See all services" button (linking to <code>/services</code>) is unaffected and works correctly. This returns "Element is not inside a CMS context" for this specific element type (a Collection List item embedded inside a Component definition), confirmed unfixable through automated means</td><td class="bad">&#10007; Broken &mdash; needs manual configuration</td></tr>
<tr><td>Separate, deeper bug found in the same "Cosmetic Treatments Patients Love" marquee (21 July 2026): the "Know more" button on each card is a Component Instance whose Link prop is not overridden per item &mdash; it silently falls back to the component's static default (the external booking-widget URL), not the treatment page at all</td><td>Traced via a manual configuration session; confirmed the wrapper's CMS source (deprecated Services collection) and the button's un-overridden Link prop. Attempted to repoint the wrapper source to the correct Cosmetic Dentistries collection after clearing the heading/paragraph/image bindings.</td><td>Blocked by a genuine, reproducible platform limitation: "Cannot change source: the list's item template contains bindings or nested lists" persists even with every text/image binding cleared &mdash; the blocker is the Component Instance (the button) itself sitting inside the item template, which our tools refuses to allow through regardless of binding state. <strong>Draft-only, not published</strong>: the heading/paragraph/image bindings were cleared in the unpublished draft as part of this attempt and left in that state (safe, live site unaffected &mdash; verified via live curl) pending a developer completing the rebind directly.</td><td class="bad">&#10007; Broken &mdash; needs manual configuration (draft has partial unpublished changes, see note)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Homepage marquee card links (5 cards: Orthodontics, Dental Implants, Cosmetic Dentistry, General Dentistry, Services)</td><td>Previously: saved data-model value vs. published output showed a mismatch. Re-checked live 21 July 2026 via curl against all 5 rendered hrefs.</td><td><strong>All 5 now return 200</strong> (<code>/orthodontists</code>, <code>/dentalimplant</code>, <code>/cosmetic-dentistry</code>, <code>/general-dentists</code>, <code>/services</code>) &mdash; the stale-link issue is no longer reproducible; appears to have been resolved since the original finding, most likely by a manual re-save/republish.</td><td class="ok">&#10003; Now fixed &amp; verified</td></tr>
<tr><td>21 <code>/thankyou/[slug]</code> confirmation pages (what a visitor sees after submitting the New Patient Registration / contact / service forms)</td><td>Live curl checks post-submission; page config, element tree, and CDN response headers all inspected previously; re-sampled 10 of 21 slugs live on 21 July 2026</td><td>All 10 sampled (and by extension, consistent with the full 21 previously checked) still return 404 live &mdash; a confirmed Webflow platform edge-routing bug (not a content misconfiguration). <strong>Deprioritized per client direction</strong> since these pages are excluded from the sitemap and aren't an indexing concern &mdash; but anyone who actually fills in a form still lands on a broken confirmation page</td><td class="bad">&#10007; Broken &mdash; deprioritized, not fixed</td></tr>
<tr><td>3 internal links resolving via a redirect rather than the final URL directly (<code>/dentures</code>, <code>/dentalimplant/single-implants</code>, <code>/photo-gallery</code>)</td><td>Live link-click/curl check</td><td>All 3 repointed directly to their final destination</td><td class="ok">&#10003; Fixed &amp; verified</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contact form submission (does it send, does validation work)</td><td class="na">Not tested &mdash; deliberately skipped</td><td class="na">Submitting a real test entry would send a genuine enquiry into the client's live lead/notification workflow; not done without explicit client sign-off first</td><td class="na">&#8212; Not tested</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cross-browser rendering (Safari/Firefox/Edge)</td><td class="na">Not documented</td><td class="na">No record of this being tested</td><td class="na">&#8212; Not tested</td></tr>
<tr><td>Device-specific layout/rendering beyond the mobile-menu link check above</td><td class="na">Not documented</td><td class="na">No record of a dedicated responsive/device QA pass</td><td class="na">&#8212; Not tested</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<div class="callout2 warn"><h4>Recommended follow-up</h4>Two things worth prioritising next: (1) the mega-menu category links regression &mdash;
these were fixed once already and need a fresh manual check of what actually changed, since the underlying CMS data is still correct; and
(2) a short, dedicated functional-QC pass covering contact-form submission (including validation and email delivery, with client sign-off
before sending a live test), cross-browser rendering, and device-specific layout checks &mdash; a real gap this project's documentation
doesn't otherwise cover.</div>
</div>

<div class="tab-panel" id="panel-pricing">
<div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">💷</div><div class="sumcard-body">
<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">0 known errors</span><strong>Price accuracy — every price on the site checked against the client's official 2026 sheet</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">Full site coverage, three verification passes: 210 price points across 48 canonical pricing pages, plus a complete sweep of all
241 live blog posts and all 10 London borough pages &mdash; 259 pages in total, nothing left unchecked. <strong>33 live price
corrections were made across the full history of this work</strong> (20 in the first pass, 3 in a same-day 2nd-pass recrawl, 13 in a
