<h2>Additional Notes</h2>
<ul><li>Scope of this pass: all 13 live /price-serice-category/* master pages, the /periodontists page, ~30 general-dentists/* treatment pages, the cosmetic-dentistry/orthodontists/teeth-veneers/invisalign-treatment/complex-dental-cases sections, the homepage, /about, and 2 blog posts. A full-sitemap curl scan (all 550 EN sitemap URLs, cache-busted, excluding /es/ and /pt/) was run to find every page containing a &#x27;£&#x27; character; 242 pages returned real (non-boilerplate) price text beyond the site-wide &#x27;0% finance over £250&#x27; footer line. The great majority of the remainder are blog posts with general cost-range commentary (e.g. &#x27;implants typically cost £2,000-£8,000&#x27;) rather than official price-list figures, and London borough/location pages that do not carry independent pricing (they link out to the canonical treatment pages already audited above). Given the scale (550 pages), this pass prioritised the canonical/master pricing pages plus every page directly tied to an official 2026 price-list category, rather than reconciling all 242 pages line-by-line.</li><li>One redirect found: https://maidasmiles.webflow.io/dentures returns HTTP 301 to https://maidasmiles.webflow.io/general-dentists/dentures (which returns 200 and was checked; it has no independent price content beyond the site-wide finance boilerplate).</li><li>PERIODONTAL TREATMENT — headline finding: the prior audit&#x27;s claim that &#x27;9 of 11 official periodontal line items are missing&#x27; is directionally correct but imprecise. Of the 11 official items: exactly 1 (&#x27;Periodontal assessment&#x27;, £175) has an exact, verifiable live match, on https://maidasmiles.webflow.io/periodontists. The other 10 have no live page presenting them under a matching name AND price. Two live items are thematically related but cannot be confirmed as the same items because both name and price diverge from the official list: &#x27;Periodontal Treatment&#x27; at £1,250 on /periodontists (loosely maps to Periodontal Pocket Reduction Surgery, official from £1,500/tooth) and &#x27;Gingival root coverage&#x27; at £1,450/quadrant on /price-serice-category/other-services-mhble (loosely maps to Gingival Plastic Surgery Root Coverage, official from £2,200 or £3,500). Both are priced below the corresponding official minimums and use a different pricing unit (flat/per-quadrant vs official&#x27;s per-tooth/per-arch), so they were logged as STILL_WRONG rather than assumed to be the same item.</li><li>PERIODONTAL TREATMENT — structural root cause found via direct CMS query: the &#x27;Fee Service categories&#x27; collection (13 items total, confirmed by API) has no Periodontal Treatment category at all, so there is no possible /price-serice-category/periodontal-treatment page. The single periodontal-themed item in the (deprecated, read-only) Services collection was categorised under &#x27;Other Services&#x27; instead, which is why one periodontal price surfaces on the Other Services page rather than anywhere periodontal-specific. This is a data-modelling gap, not a broken link — no /services/* URL is implicated (per project rule, Services-collection 404s are expected and out of scope).</li><li>The general-dentists/specialist-services page is a large, independently-maintained master fee table (not obviously CMS-bound, hardcoded) that duplicates most of the /price-serice-category/* content but has drifted out of sync with it in 7 places: Invisalign Consultation (shows £115, should be free), Periodontal Consultation (shows £115, should be £175), Root Canal &#x27;from&#x27; price (shows £950, should reflect the £1,050/£1,200/£1,350 tiered table used elsewhere), Hygiene Visit (£95 vs official £115), Hygiene with Dentist (£105 vs official £125), Composite bonding (£195 vs official £295), Sinus Lift (£1,500 vs official £1,950). This single page accounts for the largest concentration of STILL_WRONG findings in this dataset and is the highest-priority page for the client to fix next.</li><li>A second, independent Sinus Lift error was found on the homepage (https://maidasmiles.webflow.io) price table, showing £950 instead of £1,950 — exactly half the correct price and identical to the (correct) Bone Graft figure shown immediately below it, suggesting a copy/paste or field-mapping error in that section.</li><li>The homepage also self-contradicts on Implant-Retained Dentures: the top price table shows &#x27;From £6,500&#x27; (correct) while lower marketing copy on the SAME page states &#x27;Implant-retained dentures ... From £4,900&#x27; (incorrect).</li><li>general-dentists/root-canal has two separate errors on the same page: the hero strap-line reads &#x27;Root canals from £950&#x27; (should be at least £1,050, the page&#x27;s own Incisor price shown further down) and a &#x27;Dental crown from £900&#x27; line (should be £950 per Prosthodontics). The same £900 porcelain-bonded-crown figure also appears in the marquee/related-services strip on the /cosmetic-dentistry page, so this is not a one-off typo but a repeated wrong figure.</li><li>A recurring &#x27;related services&#x27; sidebar widget appears on at least 5 orthodontist sub-pages (metal-braces, ceramic-braces, self-ligating-braces, retainers, retainers-vivera) quoting per-arch prices for Invisalign/Metal/Ceramic/Self-ligating braces. The Ceramic Braces figure in this widget (£1,250/arch, implying £2,500 total) conflicts with both the official £3,500 combined price and the £1,750/arch figure stated in the body text of the ceramic-braces page itself.</li><li>All 13 live /price-serice-category/* pages, the /orthodontists, /cosmetic-dentistry, /cosmetic-dentistry/tooth-whitening(-costs), teeth-veneers/*, invisalign-treatment/*, and most general-dentists/* individual treatment pages were found to match the official 2026 price list exactly, with two confirmed exceptions: Surgical extraction (£450 shown on /price-serice-category/extractions vs correct £495, which IS shown correctly on general-dentists/tooth-extraction) and Root canal Premolar/Molar (£1,150/£1,250 shown on /price-serice-category/root-canal-treatment vs correct £1,200/£1,350, which IS shown correctly on general-dentists/root-canal&#x27;s own table). In both cases the /price-serice-category/* master page is the one carrying the wrong figure while a general-dentists/* page for the same treatment is correct — indicating the two content sources (Fee Service categories collection vs individual treatment CMS items) have drifted apart for these two items specifically.</li><li>Per project rules, the Services collection (id 689ce2c0899759a3492ed15e) was queried read-only and only to trace the source of the &#x27;Gingival root coverage £1,450&#x27; item; no /services/* URLs were crawled, flagged as broken, or treated as needing a routing fix.</li><li>All figures in this dataset are EN-locale only; /es/ and /pt/ paths were excluded from the sitemap URL list before any fetching began.</li><li><strong>2nd-pass recrawl (20 July 2026), shared-item conflict found and fixed:</strong> the &#x27;Scale &amp; Polish&#x27; Services item (slug <code>hygienist-visit</code>) was referenced by both the children&#x27;s and adult hygiene category pages simultaneously. A separate, correctly-priced &#x27;Hygiene Visit&#x27; item (£95) already existed in the collection but was orphaned — not included in the childrens-dentistry category&#x27;s reference list, despite its own fee-category field pointing back at that category. Fix: repointed the children&#x27;s category to the orphaned &#x27;Hygiene Visit&#x27; item, then corrected the now-adult-only &#x27;Scale &amp; Polish&#x27; item&#x27;s fee to £115. Both changes are additive/corrective-in-place (a reference repoint and a price-text correction within the approved exception), nothing was deleted.</li><li><strong>2nd-pass recrawl (20 July 2026), new out-of-scope finding:</strong> the SEO title tag on /orthodontists/ceramic-braces still reads &#x27;...From £1,250...&#x27; even though the page body was correctly fixed to £1,750 for a single arch in the first pass. Not edited, per the project rule that SEO title/meta-description edits require separate explicit re-authorization — flagged for a client decision instead.</li></ul>

<footer>Maida Smiles 2026 Price Verification — rebuilt from a fresh, independently fact-checked pass on 20 July 2026, recrawled and re-verified a second time same day with 3 fixes applied, then extended with a 3rd pass same day covering all 395 blog posts and 10 London borough pages (13 more fixes applied). Every figure traceable to a live, clickable page.</footer>

<div class="callout crit" style="border-left-color:var(--red); margin-top:20px;">
<strong>5th pass — 28 July 2026: "0 known errors" claim above was not accurate. 7 price discrepancies found and fixed, including a regression of a previously-claimed fix and one previously-flagged item resolved after re-investigation.</strong> A fresh site-wide re-audit (2 background research passes cross-checked against <code>Price list Maida Smiles 2026 .xlsx</code>, then a full 422-item sweep of the FAQ Items CMS collection) found 7 genuine errors, all now corrected and verified live:
<ul style="margin:8px 0 0;">
<li><strong>Composite Bonding — regression of the 3rd-pass fix logged above.</strong> The "Composite Bonding £195 → £295/tooth" fix claimed complete on 20 July was found still showing £195 live on two Smile Gallery pages (<a href="https://maidasmiles.co.uk/smile-gallery/facial-aesthetics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/smile-gallery/facial-aesthetics</a> and <a href="https://maidasmiles.co.uk/smile-gallery/implant-treatment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/smile-gallery/implant-treatment</a>). Root cause: the Services collection item's own <code>paragraph-h1</code> field still said £195 even though its <code>fee</code> field correctly said £295 — an internal self-contradiction within one CMS item. Fixed 28 July (price-value-only edit, within the approved Services-collection price exception, extended by explicit one-off authorisation to cover this gallery-feeding item since it falls outside the original price-service-category-page scope).</li>
<li><strong>FAQ item "Types of treatments and costs" (slug <code>black-teeth-03</code>) — two wrong prices in the same list.</strong> Composite bonding shown at £195 (corrected to £295) and White dental fillings shown at £195 (corrected to £285, the sheet's actual starting price). This is a plain FAQ Items collection entry, not Services-collection content — normal scope, no exception needed.</li>
<li><strong>Implant-Retained Denture — £4,900 shown instead of £6,500, found in a single shared Designer component ("Dental Implants Services") reused across ~15 pages</strong> (<code>/dentalimplant</code>, <code>/dentalimplant/missing-teeth</code> and its sub-pages, <code>/dentalimplant/types</code> and sub-pages, <code>/dentalimplant/procedure</code> and sub-pages, <code>/dentalimplant/consultation</code>, <code>/dentalimplant/peri-implantitis</code>, <code>/dentures/flexible-dentures</code>, <code>/dentures/loose-dentures</code>, three London-borough implant pages). One component-level fix corrected all affected pages simultaneously.</li>
<li><strong>Complex Dental Cases — duplicated "All-on-4 / £16,000" pricing row, resolved (previously flagged as out of scope, now fixed).</strong> Root cause diagnosed precisely: a shared "Table (2-column)" component, used in exactly 3 places site-wide (<code>/complex-dental-cases/turkey-teeth</code>, <code>/complex-dental-cases/dental-implant-rejection</code>, <code>/complex-dental-cases/failed-dentistry</code>), has 5 pricing rows built into its structure but only 3 are bound to real content (Implant-Retained Dentures, Implant-Supported Bridges, All-on-4) — the other 2 rows carry leftover duplicate "All-on-4 / £16,000" text with no formal content binding, clearly a copy-paste error from when the component was built. Initially misdiagnosed as a Services-collection reference issue and left flagged; re-investigated after being corrected that Complex Dental Cases is a separate, in-scope collection. Fix: hid the 2 extra unbound rows at the component-definition level (not deleted, not restructured beyond visibility) — corrects all 3 pages in one edit. Verified live: each price now appears exactly once per page.</li>
<li><strong>Same £4,900→£6,500 error, independently duplicated in a separate location:</strong> FAQ item <code>missing-teeth-04</code> ("Implant dentures from £4,900") on <code>/dentalimplant/missing-teeth</code> — a distinct, CMS-bound FAQ accordion entry not reachable via the Designer-level component fix above. Corrected separately.</li>
<li><strong>All-on-4 Implants — £10,000 shown instead of £16,000</strong> in FAQ item <code>missing-teeth-05</code> on the same page. New finding, not previously logged.</li>
<li><strong>All-on-6 Implants — £12,000 and Implant-Secured Dentures — £4,900</strong>, both found via a full sweep of all 422 FAQ Items collection entries (FAQ items <code>missing-teeth-06</code> and <code>multiple-implants-08</code>). Corrected to £16,000 and £6,500 respectively.</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin:10px 0 0;"><strong>Lesson from this pass:</strong> the same wrong figure (£4,900 for Implant-Retained Dentures) was independently copy-pasted into five separate content locations across the site — a shared Designer component and four distinct FAQ collection items. Fixing the visible instance on one page does not fix the others; a "0 errors, all checked" claim needs to specify whether it covered every content type (static Designer text, CMS RichText fields, and FAQ collection entries), not just rendered page text.</p>
<p style="margin:6px 0 0;"><strong>Update — 28 July 2026, later same day:</strong> the composite-bonding SEO title tag issue noted above has since been explicitly re-authorised and fixed — "£195 Per Tooth" → "£295 Per Tooth", price value only, title otherwise unchanged. Verified live via direct &lt;title&gt; tag inspection.</p>
</div>

</div>

