<div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill good">Complete — 13 blog posts fixed &amp; verified live, 22 Jul 2026</span><strong>Sitewide Americanism sweep</strong></div>
<div class="sumcard-text">A fresh, targeted scan of all 241 live blog posts (pattern-matched against a word list, then manually verified against each post's actual body content to exclude false positives — many initial "hits" were CSS properties like <code>color:#333</code> or shared page-chrome text, not real prose) found <strong>16 posts flagged, 13 with genuine Americanisms, 3 confirmed false positives.</strong> All 13 genuine cases were fixed and published live. Every fix is a straight spelling/grammar correction within existing copy — no content rewritten, per the project's content-parity rule, and <strong>no URL slugs were changed on any post</strong>, per the project's URL-stability rule.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard partial"><div class="sumcard-icon">🇬🇧</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill partial">New findings — 25 Jul 2026 live verification</span><strong>2 fixable Americanisms found, 2 flagged for human judgment — blog re-confirmed clean</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Scanned rendered body text of all 549 live EN pages against a curated UK/US spelling pattern list. Blog posts spot-checked only (already fully proofread in a prior session) — no new blog issues found. <strong>Fixable:</strong> <code>/dental-sedation</code> — "on plain local <em>anesthetic</em> alone" should be <em>anaesthetic</em> (inconsistent with the same page's correct "general anaesthesia" used twice elsewhere). <code>/team/mariya-dolhova</code> — "Completed Paediatric Dentistry <em>specialization</em>" should be <em>specialisation</em> (rest of the same bio correctly uses "Paediatric"). <strong>Needs human judgment, not auto-fixed:</strong> <code>/dentalimplant/complex-cases</code> contains "esthetic"/"esthetically" — but these are inside verbatim academic citation titles (real published journal/paper names, e.g. "Journal of Esthetic and restorative dentistry") — changing them would misquote the source, flagging only so a future pass doesn't "fix" a citation by mistake. "program" vs "programme" appears on several Team bio pages, some as generic nouns (safe to fix) and some possibly as the official title of a named international qualification (e.g. "International Advanced Program in Implant Dentistry") — needs a human to check each instance before editing. Previously-flagged FAQ item <code>complex-implant-01</code> ("optimize"→"optimise") could not be reproduced live — the same page already shows "To optimise aesthetics" correctly — likely already resolved. Full detail: <code>scratchpad/live-audit-2026-07-25.md</code>.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">🇬🇧</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Fixed — 25 Jul 2026</span><strong>Both flagged Americanisms fixed and published</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text"><code>/dental-sedation</code>: "anesthetic" → "anaesthetic". <code>/team/mariya-dolhova</code> (Team-Timelines CMS item): "specialization" → "specialisation". Both single-word corrections, published live. The 2 human-judgment items (academic citation titles, ambiguous "program"/"programme" instances) remain intentionally untouched.</div></div></div><div class="sumcard done"><div class="sumcard-icon">✅</div><div class="sumcard-body"><div class="sumcard-head"><span class="pill done">Live re-verified — 25 Jul 2026</span><strong>All Bucket-A fixes confirmed live via fresh curl re-crawl</strong></div><div class="sumcard-text">Fresh live check after publish: <code>/london/marylebone/emergency-dentist</code> now has exactly 1 &lt;h1&gt; (was 2). <code>/dental-sedation</code> shows "anaesthetic" (0 remaining "anesthetic" instances). All 8 repointed link targets return 200: <code>/team/dr-pedro-gutierres</code>, <code>/team/dr-claudia-lorenzo</code>, <code>/team/dr-shankar-bala</code>, <code>/blog/what-you-should-know-about-invisalign</code>, <code>/dentalimplant/consultation</code>, <code>/dentalimplant/procedure</code>, <code>/gum-disease</code>, <code>/cosmetic-dentistry</code>. Old broken href strings confirmed gone from their source pages (<code>/dentures</code>, <code>/london/cosmetic-dentist</code>, <code>/blog/gum-disease</code>).</div></div></div>
